# scripts/test-validators.sh now invokes audit-anchoring.sh with --stdout, so a normal
# gate run writes nothing here. This rule stays for the hand-run case: without --stdout
# the script still sinks its report into <target>/.claude/, and a fixture dir IS the
# target. That's a per-run artifact, not part of the fixture — never commit it.
**/.claude/_anchoring-audit.md
